IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-law`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-gate`

-- Israel: the limits on the force of a repeal, Interpretation Law 5741-1981 s 22. Limb (2) (a repeal cannot reach an
-- earlier act) is in il-interpretation-law.l4 from pass 1; this module adds limbs (1) and (3).
--
-- The hour a repeal takes effect is the hour s 21 gives (00:01 on the day it commences), so limb (1) compares a
-- moment with that hour. "Until" is s 8's: inclusive. Each rule is subject to s 1's gate and REFUSES when the Law is displaced.
-- Source: the unofficial Wikisource consolidation, ../../source/law.wiki (src:N). English glosses are mine; the Hebrew governs.

§ `Interpretation Law s 22: the limits on the force of a repeal`

§§ `Nouns`

-- A thing that a repeal might be thought to revive: a rule, regulation or appointment, valid from one moment and, if it
-- stopped being valid, until another. NOTHING in `valid until` means it never stopped before the repeal.
DECLARE `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive` HAS
    `valid from`   IS A Moment
    `valid until`  IS A MAYBE Moment

DECLARE `A right or obligation` HAS
    `it arises under the repealed law`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- A regulation measured against s 17 of the Ordinance (saved by Law s 31): of legislative effect or not, and the day it was
-- published in Reshumot, NOTHING if it has not been; and the day it was made known some other way (a newspaper, say), which s 17 does not count.
DECLARE `A regulation measured against s 17 of the Ordinance for publication` HAS
    `of legislative effect`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `published in Reshumot on`   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `published in some other way on`   IS A MAYBE DATE

-- What the unofficial consolidation of the Ordinance shows for one of its provisions (used beside Law s 31, below).
DECLARE `What the consolidated Ordinance shows` IS ONE OF
    `operative text`
    `marked repealed`
    `marked deleted`
    `no such provision`

§§ `Named refusals`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 22(1) speaks of a thing that had no validity when the repeal took effect; for a thing that was valid then, the question of reviving it does not arise` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 22(1) speaks of a thing that had no validity when the repeal took effect; for a thing that was valid then, the question of reviving it does not arise"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 22(3) speaks of a right or obligation under the repealed law` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 22(3) speaks of a right or obligation under the repealed law"

§§ `s 22(1) — a repeal cannot revive what had no validity`

-- Had validity "at the hour the repeal entered into force": from its start, up to and including its end (s 8).
-- src:127 | ביטולו של דין אין כוחו יפה –
-- src:128 | (1) להחיות דבר שלא היה לו תוקף בשעה שהביטול נכנס לתקפו;
@ref Interpretation Law s 22(1) (src:127-128)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      thing IS A `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` d `took effect:` thing MEANS
        `s 8 — the moment` (thing's `valid from`) `is up to and including` (`s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` d)
    AND CONSIDER thing's `valid until`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST m  THEN `s 8 — the moment` (`s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` d) `is up to and including` m

@ref Interpretation Law s 22(1) (src:127-128)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      thing IS A `A thing a repeal might be thought to revive`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) — a repeal commencing on` d `revives the thing:` thing `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   `s 22(1) — the thing had validity at the hour a repeal commencing on` d `took effect:` thing
         THEN `s 22(1) speaks of a thing that had no validity when the repeal took effect; for a thing that was valid then, the question of reviving it does not arise`
         ELSE FALSE)

§§ `s 22(3) — a repeal cannot affect a right or obligation under the repealed law`

-- Limb (3) says the repeal has no force "to affect a right or obligation under the repealed law". A right or obligation
-- that does not arise under the repealed law is outside the limb, and the rule REFUSES for it.
-- src:127 | ביטולו של דין אין כוחו יפה –
-- src:130 | (3) להשפיע על זכות או חיוב שלפי הדין המבוטל.
@ref Interpretation Law s 22(3) (src:127-130)
GIVEN x IS A `A right or obligation`
      matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(3) — a repeal affects the right or obligation:` x `, for` matter MEANS
    `under s 1, the Law's answer for` matter `is`
        (IF   x's `it arises under the repealed law`
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE `s 22(3) speaks of a right or obligation under the repealed law`)

§§ `Law s 31 against the consolidation of the Ordinance (fork F15)`

-- Law s 31 saves subsections (2) and (4) of section 16 of the Ordinance, and sections 17, 19 and 42. The consolidation in the
-- sources shows subsection (2) of section 16 as "(נמחקה)" (deleted) and (1), (3), (5) as "(בוטלה)" (repealed); only (4) has
-- text. Every section of the Ordinance except 1, 16, 17, 19 and 42 reads "(בוטל)" (repealed); section 1 has text, though Law s 31
-- does not save it. `s 31 — the Ordinance's section` (pass 1) answers what s 31 says and is unchanged: it answers TRUE for 16(2).
-- This function says what the consolidation shows, so a caller can see that s 31 saves a subsection the text shows struck.
-- src:ordinance:166 | (1)
-- src:ordinance:166 | (בוטלה);
-- src:ordinance:167 | (2)
-- src:ordinance:167 | (נמחקה);
-- src:ordinance:168 | (3)
-- src:ordinance:168 | (בוטלה);
-- src:ordinance:169 | (4) לא תהא תקנה סותרת הוראותיו של כל חוק;
-- src:ordinance:170 | (5)
-- src:ordinance:170 | (בוטלה).
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 16(1) to (5), as the consolidation shows them (src:ordinance:166-170)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `What the consolidated Ordinance shows`
`Ordinance consolidation — what the text shows for section` section `, subsection` subsection MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   section EQUALS 16
        THEN `the subsection of section 16 shown`
        IF   section EQUALS 1 OR section EQUALS 17 OR section EQUALS 19 OR section EQUALS 42
        THEN `operative text`
        IF   section AT LEAST 2 AND section AT MOST 43
        THEN `marked repealed`
        OTHERWISE `no such provision`
    WHERE
        `the subsection of section 16 shown` MEANS
            CONSIDER subsection
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `operative text`
            WHEN JUST sub THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF   sub EQUALS 4
                    THEN `operative text`
                    IF   sub EQUALS 2
                    THEN `marked deleted`
                    IF   sub EQUALS 1 OR sub EQUALS 3 OR sub EQUALS 5
                    THEN `marked repealed`
                    OTHERWISE `no such provision`

-- Whether s 31's list and the consolidation agree: TRUE when the provision survives the Law exactly where the consolidation shows
-- operative text. It is FALSE for section 16(2) (saved, shown deleted) and for section 1 (not saved, shown with text), and a
-- question about the whole of section 16 refuses, as it does in pass 1.
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31 and the consolidation of the Ordinance agree on section` section `, subsection` subsection MEANS
    (`s 31 — the Ordinance's section` section `, subsection` subsection `, survives the Law`)
        EQUALS
    (`Ordinance consolidation — what the text shows for section` section `, subsection` subsection EQUALS `operative text`)

§§ `Ordinance s 17 (saved by Law s 31): publication and the day validity begins`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Ordinance s 17 speaks only of regulations of legislative effect` MEANS
    REFUSE "Ordinance s 17 speaks only of regulations of legislative effect"

-- src:ordinance:173 | תקנות בנות־פעל תחיקתי יפורסמו ברשומות, ותחילת תקפן ביום פרסומן, אם אין הוראה אחרת בענין זה.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 17 (publication in Reshumot) (src:ordinance:173)
GIVEN r IS A `A regulation measured against s 17 of the Ordinance for publication`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 17 — the regulation must be published in Reshumot:` r MEANS
    r's `of legislative effect`

-- Validity begins on the day of publication, if there is no other provision on the matter; the day itself is included (it is the day
-- validity begins). A regulation of legislative effect that has not been published, and that no other provision gives a day,
-- has no day under this section, so its validity has not begun under s 17 (FALSE); the text does not say what an unpublished
-- regulation is worth otherwise. Publication some other way (a newspaper) is not publication in Reshumot and starts nothing under s 17. A regulation that is not of legislative effect is outside the section: the rule refuses.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 17 (the day validity begins) (src:ordinance:173)
GIVEN r IS A `A regulation measured against s 17 of the Ordinance for publication`
      day IS A DATE
      other IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 17 — the validity of the regulation has begun by` r `on` day `, unless another provision fixes the day:` other MEANS
    IF   r's `of legislative effect`
    THEN CONSIDER other
         WHEN JUST fixed THEN day AT LEAST fixed
         WHEN NOTHING    THEN CONSIDER r's `published in Reshumot on`
                              WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
                              WHEN JUST pub  THEN day AT LEAST pub
    ELSE `Ordinance s 17 speaks only of regulations of legislative effect`
